# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""The words and rules of the diary that writes itself (docs/diary.md, "Days").

Each game day the hero writes a short entry in the evening from what really happened. A line is about one topic of the
day; the game's events (ULyudQuests::Notify) count for topics by RULES. Every line is (ru, en, ja); Russian is the
source. The hero is a teenage boy: Russian past tense masculine, plain words, a little dry.

Slots: {0} is a name the game fills in (an item, a person, a bird, a festival, a place, a film). Russian names come in the
nominative, so a named line puts the name after a dash or a colon, never in a case of its own. {1} is how many.
Every topic needs plain lines (no name): they stand in when a name has no words in a language.
Build: python3 tools/daylog/build_daylog.py (--check to compare with the committed files).
"""

